# JSX scrub placeholders

When redacting LAN IPs, hostnames, or paths in **`.jsx` / `.tsx`**, do **not** leave raw angle-bracket placeholders in markup text.

esbuild parses `<SURFACE_LAN_IP>` as a JSX element and **fails the Vercel production build**.

## Do

```jsx
<code>https://&lt;SURFACE_LAN_IP&gt;:3000/xr</code>
{/* or */}
<code>{'https://<SURFACE_LAN_IP>:3000/xr'}</code>
```

## Do not

```jsx
<code>https://<SURFACE_LAN_IP>:3000/xr</code>
```

## OK without escaping

- Normal JS/TS **strings** and **comments** (`'<SURFACE_LAN_IP>'`, `// <DGX_LAN_IP>`)
- Markdown / `.md` docs (not parsed as JSX)

## Verify

`npm run verify:jsx-placeholders` (also runs from `npm run build` before Vite).
